('128.7.b.9.D.i',3,'Evidence that supports a central idea is best when it is:','["long and unrelated", "opinion only", "vague and general", "relevant and specific"]'::jsonb,3,'Evidence should fit the idea.','original'),
('128.7.b.9.D.i',3,'To identify the central idea of a science article, a reader looks at:','["the title, headings and repeated key ideas", "the page numbers", "only the first word", "the font"]'::jsonb,0,'These clues reveal the main idea.','original'),
('128.7.b.9.D.ii',3,'A timeline helps readers:','["find rhymes", "see the order of events", "compare opinions", "count syllables"]'::jsonb,1,'Timelines show sequence.','original'),
('128.7.b.9.D.ii',3,'A sidebar differs from the main text because it:','["replaces the headline", "is the title", "gives extra information set apart on the page", "is the conclusion"]'::jsonb,2,'Sidebars add focused information.','original'),
('128.7.b.9.D.iii',3,'Order of importance organizes information from:','["random order", "A to Z always", "oldest to newest only", "most to least important, or the reverse"]'::jsonb,3,'Importance determines the order.','original'),
('128.7.b.9.D.iii',3,'Logical order arranges ideas:','["so each idea follows sensibly from the last", "by length", "randomly", "by color"]'::jsonb,0,'Logical order makes sense step by step.','original')
